{"id":"surface:range-habitat-bighorn-sheep-2.1.0","speciesId":"species:bighorn-sheep","metric":"HABITAT_SUITABILITY_IN_RANGE","unit":"habitat class inside the supported range","sitesSurveyed":82,"sitesDetected":82,"source":{"authority":"North Ground (range and habitat profile)","title":"Bighorn sheep: habitat opportunity inside its range, methodology 2.1.0","url":"https://www.gbif.org/occurrence/search?taxon_key=2441119&country=ca&country=us&license=cc0_1_0&license=cc_by_4_0&hascoordinate=true&hasgeospatialissue=false&occurrencestatus=present&year=2000,2026&basisofrecord=human_observation&basisofrecord=preserved_specimen&basisofrecord=material_sample&basisofrecord=machine_observation&basisofrecord=observation","licence":"North Ground surface; inputs under CC BY 4.0 (Copernicus land cover), CC0 1.0 and CC BY 4.0 (occurrence records through GBIF.org) and the public domain (NOAA ETOPO 2022)","attribution":"Contains modified Copernicus Global Land Service information (2019). Buchhorn, M. et al., Copernicus Global Land Service: Land Cover 100m: collection 3: epoch 2019: Globe. Range from occurrence records published through GBIF.org (retrieved 2026-09-30) by the 15 datasets credited in content/intelligence/range-habitat/datasets.json. NOAA National Centers for Environmental Information. 2022: ETOPO 2022 15 Arc-Second Global Relief Model. doi:10.25921/fd45-gt74.","retrievedAt":"2026-09-30","verifiedAt":"2026-09-30"},"limitations":["How well the land suits bighorn sheep, inside the range records place it. Habitat, not a count of animals and not a density.","The range is ground within 25 km of places where openly licensed records confirm the species; where people rarely record wildlife, real range can be missing, and records can be wrong.","Records decide only whether ground is in the range; they never set a cell's colour, so where more people report wildlife does not become where there are more animals. Introduced and managed herds are recorded where visitors see them — parks, ranches, road edges — so herds on private land can be missing.","Unshaded ground is outside that range, rated unsuitable inside it, or open water, sea, ice or town the profile does not name as habitat. None of these is a finding that the species is absent.","Land cover is from 2019 and does not know forest age, recent fire or harvest.","Hunting geography and seasons play no part in this surface; the zone card says what is legal."],"observationPeriod":{"from":"2000-01-01","through":"2026-09-30"},"methodology":{"id":"methodology:north-ground-range-habitat","version":"2.1.0","effectiveFrom":"2026-09-30","history":[{"version":"1.0.0","detail":"First publication: range from clustered record squares, categorical habitat inside it."},{"version":"2.0.0","detail":"Ground inside the range rated unsuitable kept as its own state; water, sea, ice and town masked for profiles that do not name them; values placed on the grid nodes the renderer samples (1.0.0 sat half a cell south-west); an island rule for sedentary families; elevation and coast requirements; confidence from components rather than record counts alone. The concentrated-population rule (2 counted squares holding 300 records) was set AFTER the first 2.0.0 build declined kalij pheasant on 15,421 records in three squares of Hawaii Island: the five-square minimum was meant to refuse a handful of scattered reports, and refused a real island population instead. Recorded as set after seeing the result."},{"version":"2.1.0","detail":"Open water a profile names is drawn only within the profile's openWaterKm (else coastKm, else 5 km) of dry land, as the sea already was: under 2.0.0 mallard was painted across the middle of Lake Winnipeg. 'Water or wetland nearby' is a distance-weighted share falling to nothing at 20 km, replacing an unweighted 3 × 3 box that drew a hard-edged 0.3° square around every small lake (wild boar). Both set after seeing those surfaces. Gaps in the range no wider than the family's declared gapKm are joined by a morphological closing (grow by half the gap, shrink back), which can fill a hole between recorded places but never extend the range past its recorded edge or outside its convex hull; habitat and the masks still decide every joined cell. Set AFTER seeing the 2.0.0 alligator surface: 9,702 openly licensed records in 72 squares drew separate discs with central Florida blank — the records' sampling painted as absence. Recorded as set after seeing the result. And a correction, not a choice: each record square is now used at the size of the GBIF cell it stands for. The first reads' 0.35° squares were 1.40625° cells (GBIF aggregates 16 × 16 cells per map tile), so 2.0.0 drew ranges from a sixteenth of the ground the records covered, in bands with gaps between them."}]},"methodologyStatedAs":"Range: ground within 25 km of GBIF's 1.40625° cells holding 2+ openly licensed records since 2000, each within 150 km of another or holding 10+ on its own (82 squares, 3002 records). Habitat: each 0.1° cell's land cover read through this species' categorical profile (core 1, high 0.75, moderate 0.5, low 0.25, unsuitable 0), share-weighted, with required relationships as limiting factors; open water, sea, ice and town the profile does not name are masked. No weight is fitted.","scaleStatedAs":"Bighorn sheep: habitat opportunity. Colour is the habitat class for this species inside its range — red core, orange and yellow strong, green moderate, blue marginal. Habitat, not a count of animals.","season":{"observedSeason":"All seasons (resident habitat)","matchesHuntingSeason":true,"warning":"Habitat is read from the land, which does not change with the season; where the animals are within it can."},"model":{"id":"model:north-ground-range-habitat-bighorn-sheep","version":"2.1.0","claim":"RANGE_HABITAT","inputs":[{"id":"foundation:landcover-cgls-lc100-2019-0.1deg","hash":"sha256:37891209b4ae816931a1f6a944c5ac2d2403c00f4cbfda71cacd710a050de525"},{"id":"open occurrence records (content/intelligence/range-habitat/inputs/bighorn-sheep.records.json)","hash":"sha256:2cffdee3bb6f1c21a4f099f6377e6bee55ec590fa69a5d50d18dc669e557f2d5"},{"id":"foundation:terrain-etopo2022-0.1deg","hash":"sha256:676b594dbfa561b9ea7558fe4d537023d0e82042a0ee282051e9df53c7992d0f"}],"literature":["Alpine meadows, grassy mountain slopes and foothills close to rugged cliffs and bluffs, on drier slopes with limited snowfall. Winter range is typically about 760-1,520 m and summer range 1,830-2,590 m elevation. — North Ground's published profile of the species, citing Animal Diversity Web, University of Michigan Museum of Zoology, Bighorn sheep (Ovis canadensis)."],"reading":"Alpine meadow and grassy slopes are core; rock and shrub strong; open forest moderate; closed forest and ice marginal — and rugged relief (cliffs and bluffs) is required.","profile":{"family":"LOCAL_BIG_GAME","reachKm":25,"landCover":{"CORE":["HERBACEOUS","TUNDRA"],"HIGH":["BARE_SPARSE","SHRUB"],"MODERATE":["OPEN_FOREST"],"LOW":["CLOSED_FOREST","FOREST_UNKNOWN","SNOW_ICE"]},"edge":null,"requires":[{"feature":"RELIEF_METRES","thresholds":{"CORE":600,"HIGH":400,"MODERATE":250,"LOW":120}}],"coastKm":null,"season":null,"whyNotRangeHabitat":null},"range":{"confirmedSquares":91,"countedSquares":82,"islandSquares":4,"gapKm":null,"joinedCells":0,"recordGroup":"MAMMAL","edgeOnUnrecordedGround":0.081,"openRecords":3002,"datasets":15,"months":null},"cells":{"painted":17310,"unsuitable":3994,"masked":{"WATER":52,"BUILT":119,"SEA":147},"noData":0},"variation":{"classShares":{"MODERATE":0.376,"LOW":0.418,"HIGH":0.195,"CORE":0.011},"usefulVariation":true},"confidenceComponents":[{"component":"range evidence","holds":true,"detail":"3002 records in 82 squares (needs 300 in 30)"},{"component":"habitat concordance","holds":true,"detail":"record squares on moderate-or-better land 39 in 100 against 36 in 100 across the range (ratio 1.07; needs 1)"},{"component":"seasonal applicability","holds":true,"detail":"all-year records for a species that stays"},{"component":"source age","holds":true,"detail":"records read 2026-09-30; land cover epoch 2019 (its age is reported with the surface)"},{"component":"resolution","holds":true,"detail":"habitat at 0.1° (about 11 km); range edge from records within 25 km"}]},"grid":{"latStep":0.1,"lonStep":0.1,"south":17.55,"west":-169.95,"rows":665,"cols":1200,"registration":"CELL_CENTRE_NODES"},"cellsEncoded":{"encoding":"U8_DEFLATE_BASE64","scale":4,"r0":132,"c0":459,"rows":230,"cols":232,"data":""}}
